	<T_RDMI_METHOD COMPONENT_NAME="BIRT" METHOD_NAME="BIRT" METHOD_SEQNO="1" INTERFACE="N" MODULE="" INTERFACE_CORRECT="Y" CREATED_BY="P3100112" CREATED_ON="2011-05-10T09:37:49">
		<PHYSICAL_METHOD_NAME><![CDATA[com.usoft.birt.Start.loadJars(:0)
rep = new com.usoft.birt.ReportEngine(:0,:1,:2)]]></PHYSICAL_METHOD_NAME>
		<DESCRIPTION><![CDATA[This is the constructor method. This method must load the external jars from the BIRT runtime, and set the paths that are required in the component itself. You define the Datasource(s) of the report in the BIRT report designer, USoft is accessible through JDBC in the rules Service.

First parameter - BIRT runtime path to the ReportEngine folder. This parameter is also used to find and load the external jars.
Second parameter - a temp folder where BIRT can store temporary files.
Third parameter - image url prefix. This is optional; this parameter allows you to alter the image source URL when creating HTML reports]]></DESCRIPTION>
	</T_RDMI_METHOD>
	<T_RDMI_METHOD COMPONENT_NAME="BIRT" METHOD_NAME="GENERATEDOC" METHOD_SEQNO="1" INTERFACE="N" MODULE="" INTERFACE_CORRECT="Y" CREATED_BY="P3100112" CREATED_ON="2011-05-10T14:20:47">
		<PHYSICAL_METHOD_NAME><![CDATA[array=com.usoft.joker.Util.copyArray((O)argv, (i)"2")
rep.generateDOC(  (U):0, (U):1,([O) array )]]></PHYSICAL_METHOD_NAME>
		<DESCRIPTION><![CDATA[Creates a Word output file from a report design file. 

The first two parameters are the input filename and output filename. After the first two parameters, you can provide name, value pairs of as many parameters as you need for the report itself, for example:

- You have a report design Problem.rptdesign that has a Report parameter PROBLEM_NUMBER that accepts integer numbers and you want a report for problem numer 10.
- You can then generate a Word Document file as follows:

INVOKE 	BIRT.GenerateDOC
WITH	SELECT	'c:\birt\designs\Problem.rptdesign'
		,		'C:\birt\output\Problem.doc'
		,		'PROBLEM_NUMBER'
		,		'100']]></DESCRIPTION>
	</T_RDMI_METHOD>
	<T_RDMI_METHOD COMPONENT_NAME="BIRT" METHOD_NAME="GENERATEHTML" METHOD_SEQNO="1" INTERFACE="N" MODULE="" INTERFACE_CORRECT="Y" CREATED_BY="P3100112" CREATED_ON="2011-05-10T09:39:17">
		<PHYSICAL_METHOD_NAME><![CDATA[array=com.usoft.joker.Util.copyArray((O)argv, (i)"2")
rep.generateHTML( (U):0, (U):1,([O) array )]]></PHYSICAL_METHOD_NAME>
		<DESCRIPTION><![CDATA[Creates a HTML output file from a report design file. 

The first two parameters are the input filename and output filename. After the first two parameters, you can provide name, value pairs of as many parameters as you need for the report itself, for example:

- You have a report design Problem.rptdesign that has a Report parameter PROBLEM_NUMBER that accepts integer numbers and you want a report for problem numer 10.
- You can then generate a HTML output file as follows:

INVOKE 	BIRT.GenerateHTML
WITH	SELECT	'c:\birt\designs\Problem.rptdesign'
		,		'C:\birt\output\Problem.html'
		,		'PROBLEM_NUMBER'
		,		'100'

Notes:
- any image files generated by the document are saved in an 'images' folder, that is a direct subfolder where the output file is saved
- depending on how the report design is configured, the images are either saved within the HTML output file (as svg code), in .svg files in the images folder, or in .jpg files in the images folder.
- the third parameter in the constructor method can be used to modify the URL's generated in the HTML output file]]></DESCRIPTION>
	</T_RDMI_METHOD>
